From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:02:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: sleep: name the power words a wake found
 off

A wake writes back every power word that was on at the commit, so by
the time devices resume the words read on again. What they don't say
is which blocks lost their power on the way: a coprocessor whose word
went off lost its firmware too, and its driver then talks to a reset
block. The MTP and the AOP have no power domain in the tree and their
drivers have no restart path, so whether they keep their power through
a deep sleep decides whether the keyboard, the trackpad and the sensors
survive it.

Log, once per real sleep, the words of the PMGR and of the always-on
PMGR that were on at the commit and off at the wake. On by default;
apple_sleep.wake_words_report=0 turns it off.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
index 63ee2f93ab..317e2f750e 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/sleep.c
@@ -2791,11 +2791,47 @@ static void sleep_ps_rewake(struct apple_sleep *s)
 		s->ps_rewake_timeouts += redo_aon[i];
 }
 
+/*
+ * Which blocks lost their power across this sleep: a coprocessor whose word is listed lost its
+ * firmware as well, whatever the wake wrote back, and a driver that talks to it after the wake
+ * talks to a reset block. One line each for the PMGR and the always-on PMGR.
+ */
+static bool wake_words_report = true;
+module_param(wake_words_report, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(wake_words_report,
+		 "After a real sleep, name the power words found off that were on at the commit");
+
+static void sleep_ps_report_off(struct apple_sleep *s, const char *name,
+				const struct apple_sleep_words *w, const u32 *commit,
+				const u32 *woke)
+{
+	char buf[384];
+	int i, len = 0, off = 0;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < w->count; i++) {
+		if (!FIELD_GET(PS_TARGET, commit[i]) || FIELD_GET(PS_ACTUAL, woke[i]))
+			continue;
+		off++;
+		if (len < sizeof(buf) - 8)
+			len += scnprintf(buf + len, sizeof(buf) - len, " %#x", w->offset[i]);
+	}
+	if (off)
+		dev_info(s->dev, "%s: %d words on at the commit were off at the wake:%s\n", name,
+			 off, buf);
+	else
+		dev_info(s->dev, "%s: all words on at the commit were on at the wake\n", name);
+}
+
 static void sleep_ps_rewake_report(struct apple_sleep *s)
 {
 	const struct apple_sleep_words *all = &s->soc->ps_all, *aon = &s->soc->ps_aon_all;
 	int i;
 
+	if (READ_ONCE(wake_words_report)) {
+		sleep_ps_report_off(s, "PMGR", all, s->ps_commit, s->ps_woke);
+		sleep_ps_report_off(s, "AON PMGR", aon, s->ps_aon_commit, s->ps_aon_woke);
+	}
+
 	dev_dbg(s->dev, "power words: %u written back, %u not on in time\n", s->ps_rewoken,
 		s->ps_rewake_timeouts);
 	for (i = 0; i < all->count; i++)
